          }
        },
        "question_h4Tjkh": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is the warranty on a Net Return net?",
            "answer": "<ul><li><strong>Home and Pro Series Nets:</strong> 3 years or 250,000 shots (whichever comes first)</li><li><strong>Simulator screens, Net Guardians, covers, and accessories:</strong> 1-year warranty</li></ul><p>In addition, our modular design ensures that replacement parts are always available. If a frame tube bends or a net is damaged, you can purchase individual components rather than replacing the entire system. If you need a replacement, send us a photo of the damaged part to ensure you receive the correct version.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_kmnmHJ": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How do I set up my Net Return product?",
            "answer": "<p>Setting up your Net Return product is quick and easy, with most nets assembling in under five minutes without the need for tools. Follow these steps for a seamless setup:</p><ol><li><strong>Unpack the components</strong> and lay out the aluminum frame pieces according to the instruction manual.</li><li><strong>Connect the frame tubes</strong> using the Quick Color Connect System, ensuring a secure fit.</li><li><strong>Attach the netting</strong> by sliding the polyester sleeve over the frame.</li><li><strong>If using side barriers</strong>, connect them securely to the net.</li><li><strong>For outdoor use</strong>, position the net on stable ground and consider adding sandbags for extra stability in windy conditions.</li><li><strong>For simulator setups</strong>, attach the Sim Kit screen and darkening valance to your net.</li></ol><p>Need additional help? Visit our <a href=\"https://www.thenetreturn.com/pages/assembly\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">Assembly</span></a> page for detailed instructions on how to set up your net.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_ixyDqX": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Why choose The Net Return for golf nets and turf?",
            "answer": "<p>With over a decade of innovation and engineering, we have become the industry leader in premium golf nets, trusted by professionals like Bryson DeChambeau as well as instructors and home golfers worldwide. Here are a few reasons why:</p><ul><li><strong>Automatic Ball Return:</strong> Our golf nets return the ball automatically, eliminating setup hassle and maximizing practice time.</li><li><strong>Durability You Can Count On:</strong> Every Home net and Pro net is constructed with aircraft-grade aluminum and commercial-grade netting, designed to handle high-impact shots up to 250 mph.</li><li><strong>Multi-Sport Use:</strong> Unlike many other golf nets on the market, ours can also be used for soccer, baseball, and other sports, making them ideal for families.</li><li><strong>Simulator Compatibility:</strong> With optional Sim Kits, you can transform your Pro or Home net into a full golf simulator setup.</li><li><strong>Portable and Easy to Set Up:</strong> Our nets can be assembled in minutes without tools, making them perfect for home use, garages, and outdoor setups.</li></ul><p>With a commitment to quality, innovation, and customer satisfaction, The Net Return continues to set the standard for golf nets and training equipment.</p>"
          }
        }
